		(descr "Bourns MF-RHT polyfuse land that takes both lead pitches, plus the solder-bridge pads on the back. Left hole shared; middle hole = MF-RHT900 class (5.10 mm, up to Ihold 9 A), right hole = MF-RHT1300 class (10.20 mm, Ihold 10-13 A). Holes 1.2 mm to clear the thickest lead in the family. Bridge pads 0.9x3.0 mm, 0.3 mm apart, on B.Cu: leave the fuse off and blob them for an unfused board. Offsets generated from the KiCad Bourns footprints, not transcribed.")
